# Test + benchmark + build-tooling exclusions (added 2026-04-29).
#
# Why these matter: a single 4,788-line `tests/test_tui.py` was
# inflating PPXAIDEApp / MessageBox / ChatView whole-repo edge counts
# to 507 / 473 / 442 — 71-79% of those edges came from that one
# test file. The gpt-5.5 critique #6 read those numbers as a
# "god class" smell, and Item 1 in DEBT-INVENTORY-v1.18.2.md
# propagated the misread until production-code-only inbound
# verification on 2026-04-29 caught it.
#
# Without these exclusions, every refactoring decision based on
# whole-repo god-node ranking is biased: thoroughly-tested classes
# look "smelly" and undertested classes look "clean" — exactly
# inverted from the architectural reality.
#
# tests/ alone contributes 56.6% of all graph nodes; excluding the
# four buckets below drops the whole-repo graph from ~11,600 nodes
# to ~4,600 (−60%) and from ~47k edges to ~17k (−64%). The
# resulting graph is a clean architectural view, not a test-
# coverage map. To get test-coverage signal, run pytest --cov.
tests
benchmarks
scripts
examples
benchmarks/llm-eval/debug
benchmarks/llm-eval/results
